        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): report missing config clearly instead of misleading required-property errors",
        "body": "## What changed\n\nTwo validation paths (`validatePluginConfig` in `src/plugins/loader.ts` and config-time validation in `src/config/validation.ts`) used `value ?? {}` / `entry?.config ?? {}` to coerce undefined config into an empty object before JSON schema validation. For plugins with required schema properties (like `serverUrl` and `apiKey`), this produced misleading \"must have required property 'serverUrl'\" errors instead of a clear \"missing config\" message, causing 50+ spurious \"invalid config\" log lines during gateway startup config-reload cycles.\n\nAdded `pluginSchemaHasRequiredProperties` guard in the loader that returns a clear \"missing config\" error when config is undefined and the schema requires properties. Applied the same pattern to config-time validation: when `entry?.config` is undefined and the schema has required properties, report \"missing required config\" with the specific required field names instead of falling through to AJV with an empty object.\n\n## Why\n\nThe `?? {}` fallback masked the real problem: when `entry?.config` is undefined during config-reload or startup phases, the validation reported incorrect \"required-property\" errors that made it seem like the config was structurally invalid, when in fact the config was simply not resolved yet. This produced confusing error spam that obscured real validation issues.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n**Behavior addressed**: Plugin config validation with required schemas reports \"missing config\" instead of misleading per-property \"must have required property\" errors when config is undefined. Valid config still passes correctly.\n\n**Real environment tested**: Local checkout of openclaw/openclaw at commit 13001b3ea93, Node.js v22.22.0, Linux x64\n\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\n1. Checked `pluginSchemaHasRequiredProperties` against schema with `required: [\"serverUrl\", \"apiKey\"]` → returns `true`\n2. Checked undefined config + required schema → `validatePluginConfig` returns `{ ok: false, errors: [\"missing config\"] }`\n3. Checked undefined config + empty schema → passes correctly\n4. Checked valid config `{ serverUrl: \"https://x.com\", apiKey: \"secret\" }` + required schema → passes correctly\n\n**Evidence after fix**: Direct node evaluation terminal output confirming all three scenarios:\n```\nTest 1 (undefined + required): {\"ok\":false,\"errors\":[\"missing config\"]}\nTest 2 (undefined + empty): {\"ok\":true}\nTest 3 (defined + required): {\"ok\":true}\n```\n\n**Observed result after fix**: Undefined config with required-property schema produces clear \"missing config\" error instead of misleading \"must have required property 'serverUrl'\" per-property errors. Valid config passes validation correctly. Empty schemas still accept undefined config as before.\n\n**What was not tested**: Live gateway config-reload cycle with a real Docker/Unraid setup. The exact UnraidClaw plugin is not in the source tree; regression tests use synthetic required-config fixtures.\n\nFixes #63234",
        "branch": "fix/63234-plugin-config-validation-spam",
